anonymous_imports_allowed {
    A quoted path plus idea — for example `["../ontology.rq".attribute]` — opens that file as an ideaset.
    Every idea in the target file is in scope for that reference.
    A from-import or qualified import of the same path only binds the listed names for bare `[name]` references.
    It must not hide other ideas from a quoted-path reference.

    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-scope.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-linker.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/language/test/linking.test.ts:resolve anonymous import in bracket reference without import statement"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/linking.test.ts:quoted-path qualified idea is not limited to from-import specifiers"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/linking.test.ts:quoted-path qualified idea is not limited to a qualified import of the same file"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/linking.test.ts:sqlite-schema quoted path reaches indexer ideas that are not from-imported"]
    )
}

unused_imports {
    An import binding that is never referenced by any local reference in the importing file is unused.
    A `from "path" import idea` binds `idea`; a `from "path" import idea as alias` binds `alias`; `import "path" as ns` binds `ns`; `import "path".ideaset.idea [as alias]` binds `alias` or `idea`; a bare `import "path"` (no `as`) binds nothing and is always unused since anonymous references (`["path".idea]`) never need it.
    Used names are those that appear as `Local` (`[name]` / `[[name]]` or `[qualifier.idea]` with qualifier = alias) or as `IdeaSet` members (`ideaset foo { member1, member2 }`).
    The severity is configurable per `.reqlan/config.json` (`unusedImports`: `"warn"` | `"error"` | `"off"`, default `"warn"`) and via VS Code setting `reqlan.unusedImports`. The `reqlan.check` CLI accepts `--unused-imports <warn|error|off>`, overriding the config for that run.
    When set to `warn`, emit `warning`; when `error`, emit `error`; when `off`, suppress the diagnostic entirely.
    Lines preceded by `//rq-ignore-error` suppress the unused import diagnostic, matching ["./syntax.rq".comment_reference_ignore].
    Editor: emit `DiagnosticTag.Unnecessary` so VS Code dims/fades the line; provide a Quick Fix (`Remove unused import`) that removes the specifier (with its comma) for `from` imports or the entire import line for namespace/qualified/bare imports.
    Related: [import_tokenisation], [anonymous_imports_allowed], ["../extension/language/support/features-imports.rq".import_does_not_exist_error], ["../extension/host/configuration.rq".configuration_import_roots].

    @status in-progress
    @implementation (
        ["../../packages/extension/schemas/config.schema.json"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/src/ast.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/check/imports.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-lsp/src/analysis.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-lsp/src/code_actions.rs"]
        ["../../packages/extension/package.json"]
        ["../../packages/cli/src/commands/check.ts"]
    )
}

import_tokenisation {
    if an import is given an alias, then the base name is still available as a variable name and should not cause a conflict.
    Only the alias binds in the importing file; the imported idea's base name may be reused for a local idea.
    e.g.
    ```.rq
    from "example.rq" import myidea as examplealiasedidea

    myidea {
        this should not cause a conflict.
    }
    ```
    The same rule applies to qualified imports with `as`.
    Unaliased imports still bind the idea name and conflict with a local idea of that name.
    Related: ["../extension/language/syntax/features-syntax.rq".sensible_alias_support].

    @tests (
        ["../../packages/language/test/validating.test.ts:allows local idea when import uses an alias"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/validating.test.ts:allows local idea when qualified import uses an alias"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/validating.test.ts:reports duplicate when local idea shares unaliased import binding"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/linking.test.ts:import idea reference resolves to imported file when local idea shares name"]
    )
    @implementation (
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan.langium"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-import-bindings.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-validator.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-scope.ts"]
    )
}

wildcard_references {
    Qualified path + idea-pattern references match multiple ideas across files.
    Surface forms: bracket `[…]` and wikilink `[[…]]` (same `WildcardReference` target).
    Path is a quoted string that may include shell-style globs (`*`, `**`, `?`) and `@/` import-root aliases
    ([configuration_import_root_alias]). Relative globs resolve against the defining document directory;
    `.` / `..` segments are collapsed before matching.
    Idea pattern is an unquoted `WILDCARD_NAME` that must contain at least one `*` or `?`
    Exact quoted-path plus idea stays ["./syntax.rq".reference_qualified].
    Matching uses anchored globs (not full JS regex): path `*` is one segment, `**` crosses segments;
    idea `*` / `?` match within the idea name.
    Zero matches produce a warning diagnostic. One match also produces a warning — a wildcard is for many ideas;
    use a concrete ["./syntax.rq".reference_qualified] when only one idea matches
    (["../core_analysis/check.rq".check_wildcard_one]).
    Path segment `/**/` must not be lexed as an empty block comment — see ["./syntax.rq".comments].
    Lexer note: `ID` is a prefix of many wildcard names (`import_` vs `import_*`); the token builder
    sets `ID.LONGER_ALT = WILDCARD_NAME` so `import_*` is one token. Body prose `*` tokens are accepted
    via `WILDCARD_NAME` in PlainText so ordinary `*` characters still parse.
    Without that longer-alt, a live wildcard inside a block body can fail Idea recovery and leave later
    top-level ideas unindexed (soft mtime sync will not rebuild until the `.rq` file changes).
    Navigation does not emit N LocationLinks. A document-link click opens
    `reqlan.openWildcardReference` with `{ pathPattern, ideaPattern, fromUri }` (see [wildcard_references_webview]).
    Go-to-definition does not open that panel.
    Indexing fans out per ["../indexer/indexer.rq".wildcard_reference_edges]
    (owned under ["../indexer/indexer.rq".index]): native extract writes one `wildcard_reference`
    edge per catalog match; empty catalog / zero matches → one unresolved edge of that kind
    labeled with the pattern text. ["../core_analysis/check.rq".check] handles 0-match and 1-match fan-out
    through ["../core_analysis/check.rq".check_wildcard_zero] and ["../core_analysis/check.rq".check_wildcard_one]
    (["../core_analysis/check.rq".check_wildcard_sparse]).
    Ideas Summary graph toggles those edges via
    ["../extension/workspace-summary/ideas_summary/graphical_graph.rq".wildcard_refs_toggle].
    The server can answer `reqlan/wildcardReferenceAt`. Go-to-definition does not call it.
    Related: ["./syntax.rq".reference_embedding], ["./syntax.rq".reference_brackets], ["./syntax.rq".reference_wikilink],
    ["../indexer/indexer.rq".wildcard_reference_edges], ["../core_analysis/check.rq".check_wildcard_sparse],
    ["../core_analysis/check.rq".check_wildcard_zero], ["../core_analysis/check.rq".check_wildcard_one].

    Illustrative forms (fenced so this file does not embed live wildcards):
    ```
    ["../extension/**/*.rq".*_pane]
    ["./modules/*.rq".import_*]
    [["./mods/*.rq".widget_*|widgets]]
    ```

    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan.langium"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-wildcard-resolve.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-token-builder.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-validator.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-file-link-resolver.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-definition-provider.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-document-link-provider.ts"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/extract.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/sync.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/extract.rs"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/src/index-store/workspace-index-file.ts"]
        ["../../packages/extension/src/language/main.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/language/test/wildcard-references.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/wildcard-references.test.ts:e2e: tokenize → parse → resolve → document link → definition → command args"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/wildcard-references.test.ts:e2e: ** path glob matches nested fixture files"]
